# Who has to approve a change before it can land on main.
#
# GitHub reads this file when a pull request is opened and asks the owner of
# every touched path for a review. The ruleset on main refuses to merge until
# that review is an approval, so this file is where "with my approval" lives.
#
# One line, on purpose: every path, one approver. Add a line above it for a
# path someone else should own, and the more specific pattern wins.

